          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly and emphatically avows the speaker's present love for Maria. Its asseverative setting presents that emotional state as unquestionably true in answer to her doubt.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves assert love rather than undertake a future action or relational obligation. The longer turn contains separate language about living and dying with Maria, but that neighbouring commitment must not be transferred onto the marked avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is highly emotional, the focal expression is a deliberate, syntactically framed answer to Maria's question, not a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"Its core force is adequately represented as a solemn truth-presenting avowal. Its reassuring effect in context does not establish a distinct residual mode beyond T.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent change is genuine and lasting rather than temporary longing for his lover. He answers her directly with the focal solemn avowal, embedded in a longer declaration.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression makes no undertaking; it avows love. The surrounding turn separately presents an enduring shared-life orientation, especially in “Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.” Maria's tears and happiness show that she understands and accepts the avowal as truthful, though the passage does not record a separate explicit acceptance of defined commitment terms.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere through the narrator's prior reflection and the statement that Maria understands he speaks truly. Nevertheless, the supplied evidence alone does not establish formal commitment terms or their later fulfilment.\"}"
